    "heading": "1. What Is Software? [Spec 1.3.1]",
    "id": "h-1",
    "text": "📋 SPEC 1.3.1 Be able to identify the purpose of system software and application software. Software is the collective name for programs, data and instructions that tell computer hardware what to do. Without software, hardware is completely useless. There are two fundamental categories: S O F T W A R E ▼ SYSTEM SOFTWARE APPLICATION SOFTWARE Operating System Manages hardware & resources Utility Software Maintenance & protection Communication Software Remote access & messaging General Purpose Many different tasks Special Purpose One specific task only 💡 The Golden Rule for Classification System software: Manages the computer itself — runs in the background; the user rarely interacts with it directly. If it helps RUN the computer, it is system software. Application software: Performs tasks directly for the end user. If the user actively uses it to DO something (write, calculate, browse, edit), it is application software. Common trap: Antivirus software is SYSTEM software (utility) — NOT application software. It maintains the computer, not the user's work."
