    "heading": "9. Practice Questions",
    "id": "h-9",
    "text": "Answer all questions in full sentences. Use the command word to guide your response — 'state' needs no explanation; 'describe' needs detail; 'explain' needs a reason; 'discuss' needs both sides. Section A — State & Define [1–2 marks each] Q Question Marks Skill 1 State what is meant by the term 'software'. 1 State 2 State the difference between system software and application software. 2 State 3 State two examples of utility software. 2 State 4 State what is meant by 'open source software'. 1 State 5 State one difference between a single-user OS and a network OS. 1 State 6 State the purpose of print spooling. 1 State 7 State what is meant by 'communication software'. [Spec 1.3.6] 1 State 8 State two reasons why software developers release updates. 2 State Section B — Describe & Explain [2–4 marks each] Q Question Marks Skill 9 Describe two functions of an operating system. [Spec 1.3.3] 4 Describe 10 Explain how print spooling works and why it is useful in a school with 30 computers sharing one printer. [Spec 1.3.3] 4 Explain 11 Explain the purpose of communication software. Give one real-life example. [Spec 1.3.6] 3 Explain 12 Describe the difference between open source and proprietary software. Give one advantage of each. [Spec 1.3.5] 4 Describe 13 Explain why software needs to be updated regularly. Give THREE different reasons. [Spec 1.3.7] 6 Explain 14 Describe how automatic software updates work on a user's computer. [Spec 1.3.7] 3 Describe 15 Describe TWO risks to a user's data or system when software is updated. [Spec 1.3.7] 4 Describe 16 Explain the difference between control software and project management software. Give an example of each. [Spec 1.3.4] 4 Explain 17 Explain the difference between general purpose and special purpose application software, giving one example of each. [Spec 1.3.4] 4 Explain Section C — Scenario & Extended Response [4–6 marks each] Q Question Marks Skill 18 A primary school IT manager is choosing between an open source operating system (Linux) and a proprietary operating system (Windows). Evaluate which option is more suitable for the school. Give reasons for your answer. [Spec 1.3.5] 6 Evaluate 19 A hospital is deciding between custom-written and off-the-shelf software for its patient booking system. Discuss the advantages and disadvantages of each option for this organisation. [Spec 1.3.5] 6 Discuss 20 A large engineering firm has 500 employees working from offices in five different countries. They need software to communicate and collaborate in real time. Describe TWO types of communication software that would be suitable and explain how each would help. [Spec 1.3.6] 4 Describe 21 A software company releases a major update to a widely used accounting package used by 10,000 businesses. Explain TWO risks this update could cause and describe how each risk could be reduced. [Spec 1.3.7] 6 Explain 22 A school network of 250 computers needs an operating system. The school has one IT technician. Explain which type of operating system would be most suitable and give TWO specific benefits of that choice. [Spec 1.3.3] 4 Explain 23 A manufacturing company uses control software to manage its factory robots. Explain what control software is and describe TWO advantages it provides over manual operation of the robots. [Spec 1.3.4] 4 Explain"
