    "heading": "10. Choosing the Right Device — Scenario Practice",
    "id": "h-10",
    "text": "The exam will give you a scenario and ask you to recommend a device or storage medium. Use this table to practise the decision-making process. Scenario Best Device/Medium Key Justification A bank needs to archive 10 years of financial transaction records cheaply and securely Magnetic tape Cheapest cost per GB for large-scale archival; data rarely needs to be accessed quickly A photographer wants to transfer 50 high-resolution photos from their camera to a laptop SD card + card reader Built into camera; compact; fast enough for photo files; plug-and-play A school wants to run an OS from fast storage for 200 student laptops Internal SSD Very fast boot times; reliable; no moving parts; handles frequent read/write cycles A student needs to carry a 2GB project file between home and school USB flash drive Small; portable; works on any computer with USB port; adequate speed for 2GB A video production company needs to edit 4K footage with no lag High-capacity internal SSD Fastest read/write speeds; no lag during editing; can handle large file sizes A cinema releases a new 4K film to customers as a physical disc Blu-ray BD-R disc Capacity of 50–100GB needed for 4K; BD-R cannot be altered after burning — prevents copying A primary school wants all students to mark answers on paper exam sheets for automatic marking OMR reader + forms Optical mark recognition reads pencil marks; fast automated marking; no typing needed A supermarket needs to track stock levels automatically when items are sold Barcode scanner at checkout Reads product barcode; reduces stock count in database automatically; fast and accurate A hospital needs to identify patients quickly and securely without cards that can be lost Biometric scanner Fingerprint or iris scan is unique; cannot be lost or forgotten; very secure identity verification 🎯 Scenario Answer Framework Step 1. Name the device/medium: Be specific ('inkjet printer', 'BD-R disc', 'USB flash drive'). Step 2. Name the key feature: Match a specific characteristic to the scenario requirement. Step 3. Explain HOW: Say why that feature matters in THIS particular situation. Step 4. Repeat: Give a second reason with a DIFFERENT feature for 4-mark answers. Example: 'A Blu-ray BD-R disc (1) — it has a capacity of up to 100 GiB (1), which is large enough to store a 4K film (1). The BD-R format can only be written once (1), which means the film content cannot be altered after manufacturing, protecting it from unauthorised copying (1).'"
