    "text": "Answer all questions in full sentences. For Section C, always name the specific hardware/software and then justify with 'because' linked to the scenario. Section A — State & Define [1–2 marks each] Q Question Marks Skill 1 State what the abbreviation 'RAM' stands for and state ONE purpose of RAM. 2 State 2 State what the abbreviation 'ROM' stands for and state ONE characteristic of ROM. 2 State 3 State ONE difference between RAM and ROM. 1 State 4 State what is meant by 'volatile' memory. 1 State 5 State how processor speed is measured. 1 State 6 State ONE example of a device that uses flash memory. 1 State 7 State what happens to data in RAM when the computer is switched off. 1 State 8 State what the ALU does inside a CPU. 1 State Section B — Describe & Explain [2–4 marks each] Q Question Marks Skill 9 Describe TWO characteristics of RAM. [Spec 1.6.2] 4 Describe 10 Explain why ROM is necessary for a computer to function. [Spec 1.6.2] 3 Explain 11 Describe THREE stages of the Fetch-Decode-Execute cycle. [Spec 1.7.1] 3 Describe 12 Explain TWO factors (other than clock speed) that affect the performance of a computer. [Spec 1.7.2] 4 Explain 13 Describe the difference between flash memory and RAM. [Spec 1.6.2 & 1.6.3] 4 Describe 14 Explain what happens when a computer's RAM becomes full. [Spec 1.6.2] 3 Explain 15 Describe the role of the Control Unit and the ALU in the CPU. [Spec 1.7.1] 4 Describe 16 Explain why a larger amount of RAM improves computer performance. Give one example. [Spec 1.6.2] 3 Explain 17 Explain the difference between a computer's RAM and its storage drive. [Spec 1.6.2] 4 Explain Section C — Scenario Questions [4–6 marks each] Q Question Marks Skill 18 A professional film editor needs a computer to edit 4K video files. Recommend FOUR specific hardware components for this system. For each, state an appropriate specification and justify why it is needed. [Spec 1.7.1 & 1.8.1] 8 Justify 19 A school is buying 30 laptops for students aged 11–16 who will use them for word processing, internet research, and creating presentations. Identify THREE hardware features that should be prioritised and justify each choice. [Spec 1.8.1 & 1.8.4] 6 Justify 20 A partially sighted adult uses a computer at home for reading e-books and browsing the internet. Identify TWO hardware adjustments and TWO software settings that could be configured to help this user. Justify each choice. [Spec 1.8.1 & 1.8.3] 8 Justify 21 Discuss whether increasing clock speed (GHz) alone is sufficient to significantly improve the performance of a modern computer system. [Spec 1.7.2] 4 Discuss 22 A software developer works from home and needs to run multiple virtual machines simultaneously, compile large code bases, and attend video conferences. Recommend a complete hardware configuration for this user, justifying each component. [Spec 1.8.1 & 1.8.4] 6 Recommend 23 A student says: 'I need more storage because my computer is running slowly.' Explain whether the student has correctly identified the problem and suggest what upgrade would actually help. [Spec 1.6.2] 4 Explain 24 A company is setting up a call centre with 50 workstations. Each agent will use a customer database, make VoIP calls, and access a cloud-based CRM system. Recommend suitable hardware and software, justifying each choice. [Spec 1.8.1 & 1.8.2] 6 Recommend"
