    "text": "📋 SPEC 6.4 Use templates; insert text/images/buttons/animation; format headings/subheadings/body text/alignment; HTML: hyperlinks, images, font enhancements. 5.1 Web Page Features Web Authoring Element Description Spec Requirement Template Pre-designed web page layout with placeholder areas for content — ensures consistent design Use existing template; modify content areas; keep structural elements Tables / Frames HTML structures dividing the page into layout sections Use table structure for page layout; grid system for columns Standard page features Header banner; navigation menu; main content area; footer Every professional page has these zones; use template placeholders Navigation / Menu Links to other pages of the website — horizontal or vertical menu All pages must be navigable; use hyperlinks; test all links work Text content Headings (h1–h6); sub-headings; body text paragraphs Correct hierarchy: h1 for page title; h2 for sections; p for body Images Insert and position images with appropriate alt text Use JPG/PNG for photos; ensure images are appropriately sized Buttons Clickable navigation or action elements Buttons can link to pages, email, or trigger actions Animation Basic CSS or GIF animations to add visual interest Subtle animation — avoid excessive movement that distracts Alignment Left, centre, right alignment of text and elements Consistent alignment improves readability 5.2 HTML Reference — Key Tags HTML Tag Purpose Example text Hyperlink — links text to another page Contact Us Insert image with alt text description text or text Bold text formatting Important text or text Italic text formatting Scientific name text Underlined text Terms and Conditions text to Heading levels — h1 largest, h6 smallest Welcome to our site text Paragraph of text This is the first paragraph. Line break (no closing tag needed) End of line Start of next line item Unordered (bulleted) list First item Second item Ordered (numbered) list Step one Step two data HTML table structure Creates table > row > cell structure content Division/section container for layout Header content 📋 HTML Structure — Essential Framework Page title shown in browser tab Main heading Body text paragraph Link to page 2 Description\"> Closing tag — ALL tags must be properly closed"
